  ],
  "notes": "Composed of {鎮|ちん} (to calm, suppress) + {定|てい} (to settle, fix). A formal literary word more commonly found in historical texts and official documents than in everyday conversation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {反乱|はんらん}を{鎮定|ちんてい}する: to suppress a rebellion\n- {騒乱|そうらん}を{鎮定|ちんてい}する: to quell a disturbance\n- {鎮定|ちんてい}に{当|あ}たる: to be assigned to pacification\n- {鎮定|ちんてい}{後|ご}: after pacification\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {鎮圧|ちんあつ}: suppression — emphasizes the use of force; more commonly used\n- {平定|へいてい}: subjugation, pacification — bringing an entire region under control\n- {鎮静|ちんせい}: calming, tranquilization — gentler; also used for medical sedation",
